course: dictionary
lesson: 3595
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Fiendish is one of these words. Its first meaning is very cruel or wicked, like a fiend, which is a devil or evil spirit. Its second, informal meaning is extremely clever, complicated or difficult.
explain: «Ruby refused a PEGI 7 game as babyish, and it turned out to be a fiendish puzzle game that beat her dad.» Could a game be cruel? Not really. A game that beats a grown-up must be very hard, so here fiendish means difficult. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: In a story, a villain might make a fiendish plan, and then the word means cruel and wicked. A teacher might set a fiendish riddle, and then it means very hard. Phrases such as «fiendishly difficult» also show the hard meaning. The words around fiendish are the clues that tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Fiendish is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a fiendish plan, a fiendish puzzle.
fact: «Fiendish» means very cruel or wicked, like a fiend.
fact: Informally, «fiendish» means extremely clever, complicated or difficult.
fact: «Fiendishly difficult» means very, very hard.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, so always check the context before you choose one.
exercise: «Ruby refused a PEGI 7 game as babyish, and it turned out to be a fiendish puzzle game that beat her dad.» What does fiendish mean here? | Babyish and silly | *Extremely hard to solve | Cruel and wicked, like a devil | Very wet and grey
exercise: In a story, the villain makes a fiendish plan to steal the crown. What does fiendish mean here? | Very easy to follow | Happy and kind | *Cruel and wicked | Bright and shiny
exercise: Which sentence uses fiendish in the cruel sense? | My fiendish brother loves cake | *The fiend's fiendish plan was to ruin the whole village | The fiendish sudoku had only one solution | A fiendish puzzle kept me awake all night
test: Which word could replace fiendish in «a fiendish puzzle» without changing the meaning? | *Tricky | Easy | Lovely | Wet
test: Why does the clue «that beat her dad» tell you fiendish means hard? | Because puzzles are always wicked | Because dads are cruel | It doesn't; it means babyish | *Because a game that beats a grown-up must be very difficult
exam: In a story, a villain plots a fiendish scheme to hurt the town. What does fiendish mean? | Very friendly | Very sleepy | Very small | *Very cruel and wicked
